From ae934bf6c37f50e2925656d320dccd633c7067eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:26:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] socket, netdb: AF_INET6 sockets, AAAA lookups, IPv6 name
 servers

AF_INET6 sockets use the same tcp and udp schemes, with the address in
brackets. getaddrinfo asks for AAAA records too (A first for AF_UNSPEC)
and returns sockaddr_in6. The resolver tries every name server, IPv4 or
IPv6 from /etc/net/dns, then those from /scheme/netcfg/resolv/nameserver6,
with a 5 s timeout each, and closes its socket.
